<title>JAPAN: Obayashi wins Y42 bln Sydney Olympic stadium order.</title>
<headline>Obayashi wins Y42 bln Sydney Olympic stadium order.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Obayashi Corp said on Monday it had received an order worth about 42 billion yen to build a stadium for the 2000 Olympic Games in Sydney.</p>
<p>The order, awarded by the New South Wales government, was won by a consortium set up by Obayashi and three Australian partners.</p>
<p>The other members of the consortium are Multiplex Construction Pty Ltd, merchant bank Hambros Australia and Macquarie Corporate Finance.</p>
<p>An Obayashi spokesman said Obayashi and Multiplex would do the actual work, with Multiplex working as a subcontractor.</p>
</text>
